INTUITION

We want to rearrange the linked list so that nodes at odd positions come first, followed by nodes at even positions.
Example:
1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5

Odd positions:
1 → 3 → 5

Even positions:
2 → 4

Final result:
1 → 3 → 5 → 2 → 4

APPROACH

1. Keep an odd pointer for odd-position nodes.
2. Keep an even pointer for even-position nodes.
3. Connect each odd node to the next odd node.
4. Connect each even node to the next even node.
5. Save the first even node using evenHead.
6. At the end, connect the odd list to the even list.

COMPLEXITY

Time: O(n) — each node is visited once.
Space: O(1) — only a few pointers are used.
 
class Solution {
    public ListNode oddEvenList(ListNode head) {
        if (head == null) return null;

        ListNode odd = head;
        ListNode even = head.next;
        ListNode evenHead = even;

        while (even != null && even.next != null) {
            odd.next = even.next;
            odd = odd.next;

            even.next = odd.next;
            even = even.next;
        }

        odd.next = evenHead;

        return head;
    }
}
